title: nemesis1_messenger
---
Narrator:
The messenger speaks for exactly three minutes.

---

Narrator:
They are a person, not a recording. They have a title you don't recognise and use it without explanation.

They say: you have come further than your predecessors. That is noteworthy. That is the reason for this conversation.

---

Narrator:
They say: we are not your enemy yet. Whether we become one depends on what you do next. Not here. In the systems that follow.

They say: we will know what you decide.

They say: we will reach out again.

---

Narrator:
Then the channel closes.

---

Narrator:
Your security officer spends the next two hours compiling everything she knows about what just spoke to you.

At the end of the two hours, she concludes: not much.

---

-> [File the exchange as classified intelligence]
    <<apply_effect "nemesis_intel">>
    Narrator:
    The dossier is sealed under your command authority.

    Narrator:
    Whatever the nemesis is, you now have the beginning of a picture.

    Narrator:
    Your security officer says: first contact. Whether it's the good kind, we won't know for a while.

-> [Treat it as a threat — prepare countermeasures]
    <<apply_effect "nemesis_curse">>
    Narrator:
    You order full counter-intelligence protocols. New transponder signatures. Randomised routing.

    Narrator:
    Whatever they were assessing, you're done being assessed.

    Narrator:
    Three days later, your navigation systems start throwing minor errors. Nothing critical.

    Narrator:
    Nothing provable.

===
